==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tempten}}, from {{der|en|fro|tempter}} (French: {{m|fr|tenter}}), from {{der|en|la|tempto|temptare}}, from {{m|la|tento|tentare|to handle, touch, try, test, tempt}}, frequentative of {{m|la|tendo|tendere|to stretch}}. Displaced native {{cog|en|costning||temptation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tɛmpt/|/tɛmt/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tempt.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛmpt|ɛmt|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provoke]] someone to do [[wrong]], especially by [[promising]] a [[reward]]; to [[entice]].
#: {{syn|en|entice|fand|lure|pander|tease}}
#: {{ux|en|She '''tempted''' me to eat the apple.}}
#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|i|2|By Heav’ns, ſuch Virtues, join’d with ſuch Succeſs,<br>Diſtract my very Soul: Our Father’s Fortune<br>Wou’d almoſt '''tempt''' us to renounce his Precepts.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=Claire A. Culleton|title=Names and Naming in Joyce
|passage=Eveline Hill, the protagonist of the Dubliners story "Eveline," for example, successfully extricates herself from the confines of her "Eve" name since, like her nameling in the Garden of Eden who was '''tempted''' by promises of knowledge, Eveline, too, is '''tempted''': {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[attract]]; to [[allure]].
#: {{syn|en|beguile|entrance|Thesaurus:allure}}
#: {{ux|en|Its glossy skin '''tempted''' me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008 |title=How to Tempt a Fish: A Complete Guide to Fishing |author=Popular Mechanics |page=20 |ISBN=|passage=The next time you are trout fishing and none of your lures '''tempts''' the fish, smoke a spoon hook and cast it.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provoke]] something; to [[court]].
#: {{syn|en|foment|urge|Thesaurus:incite}}
#: {{ux|en|It would be '''tempting''' fate.}}

